1
00:00:03,130 --> 00:00:04,830
<i>In this world...</i>

2
00:00:05,300 --> 00:00:10,670
<i>Is the destiny of mankind controlled by some transcendental entity or law?</i>

3
00:00:11,360 --> 00:00:14,530
<i>Is it like the hand of God hovering above?</i>

4
00:00:15,510 --> 00:00:17,340
<i>At least it is true...</i>

5
00:00:17,810 --> 00:00:21,370
<i>...that man has no control, even over his own will.</i>

6
00:00:27,590 --> 00:00:32,750
I beseech anyone who can stop
the march of Tudor's black devils...

7
00:00:39,740 --> 00:00:41,200
D-Don't break up your formation!

8
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:42,170
Encircle him!

9
00:00:44,440 --> 00:00:45,200
T-They are...

10
00:00:45,610 --> 00:00:46,840
The Band of the Hawk!

11
00:00:47,240 --> 00:00:51,010
The Grim Reapers of the Battlefield
led by the White Hawk, Griffith!

12
00:01:12,420 --> 00:01:14,510
Feel no shame about shape

13
00:01:14,590 --> 00:01:16,430
Weather changes their phrase

14
00:01:16,550 --> 00:01:20,180
Even mother will show you another way

15
00:01:20,180 --> 00:01:22,560
So put your glasses on

16
00:01:22,640 --> 00:01:24,640
Nothing will be wrong

17
00:01:24,730 --> 00:01:26,850
There's no blame. There's no fame

18
00:01:26,850 --> 00:01:28,690
It's up to you

19
00:01:28,850 --> 00:01:32,320
The first words should be found

20
00:01:32,940 --> 00:01:35,950
Whatever holds you back

21
00:01:36,820 --> 00:01:37,320
I...

22
00:01:37,700 --> 00:01:38,450
...can...

23
00:01:38,530 --> 00:01:40,620
I can get it off

24
00:01:40,620 --> 00:01:41,620
Tell me what...

25
00:01:41,620 --> 00:01:42,620
Tell me what...

26
00:01:42,620 --> 00:01:44,450
Tell me what you want

27
00:01:44,580 --> 00:01:45,540
I don't know why...

28
00:01:45,750 --> 00:01:46,540
Don't know why...

29
00:01:46,540 --> 00:01:48,540
Don't know why you're afraid

30
00:01:48,710 --> 00:01:49,710
Tell me what...

31
00:01:49,790 --> 00:01:50,670
Tell me what...

32
00:01:50,840 --> 00:01:52,340
Tell me what you'd say

33
00:01:52,590 --> 00:01:53,670
I don't know why...

34
00:01:53,800 --> 00:01:54,760
Don't know why...

35
00:01:54,840 --> 00:01:55,550
Too late...

36
00:01:55,630 --> 00:01:57,170
It's too late

37
00:02:02,100 --> 00:02:06,100
A Wind of Swords

38
00:02:46,520 --> 00:02:48,480
R-Retreat, retreat!

39
00:03:04,580 --> 00:03:05,580
Y-Your Majesty!

40
00:03:40,030 --> 00:03:42,280
Captain! Captain Guts!

41
00:03:42,490 --> 00:03:44,530
It was amazing, Captain!

42
00:03:44,530 --> 00:03:46,240
You took them in one charge!

43
00:03:46,240 --> 00:03:47,790
That was something else!

44
00:03:47,790 --> 00:03:50,200
Nothing less from our raider commander!

45
00:03:50,200 --> 00:03:52,290
You're our boss, all right!

46
00:03:53,670 --> 00:03:56,590
You did a good job too...

47
00:03:56,590 --> 00:03:58,210
Sorry, I got a little carried away.

48
00:03:58,550 --> 00:04:00,010
No need to apologize.

49
00:04:00,010 --> 00:04:03,630
We get to brag about our
commander to everyone else!

50
00:04:03,630 --> 00:04:04,760
He's right!

51
00:04:04,760 --> 00:04:07,510
Now let's have a drink to celebrate!

52
00:04:07,850 --> 00:04:08,890
Captain Guts!

53
00:04:13,140 --> 00:04:14,560
Big sister Casca...

54
00:04:16,520 --> 00:04:17,820
Commander Casca!

55
00:04:18,230 --> 00:04:19,650
We need to talk.

56
00:04:19,650 --> 00:04:23,280
Can I have your ear for a minute, Captain Guts?

57
00:04:24,070 --> 00:04:25,990
Hey, start without me.

58
00:04:25,990 --> 00:04:27,200
I'll catch up.

59
00:04:30,200 --> 00:04:31,410
What's going on?

60
00:04:31,410 --> 00:04:33,000
They're going to start arguing again.

61
00:04:33,750 --> 00:04:36,750
It's probably over
the captain's lone charge into battle.

62
00:04:38,170 --> 00:04:39,920
What did you think you were doing?

63
00:04:39,920 --> 00:04:40,710
About what?

64
00:04:40,710 --> 00:04:41,710
Don't give me that!

65
00:04:41,710 --> 00:04:44,590
Our plan was to support
the main force's charge...

66
00:04:44,590 --> 00:04:48,720
...while our companies each cover
a flank and contain the enemy attack.

67
00:04:48,720 --> 00:04:50,850
Despite your success...

68
00:04:50,850 --> 00:04:53,810
...you ruined our battle plans, charging
alone into the center of the enemy!

69
00:04:54,350 --> 00:04:57,230
Who do you think you are, some hero?

70
00:04:57,440 --> 00:05:00,150
Even though we were lucky this time...

71
00:05:00,150 --> 00:05:04,780
Your selfish actions could put all of
the Band of the Hawk in real danger!

72
00:05:06,070 --> 00:05:08,410
Try to keep your position in mind sometimes!

73
00:05:12,750 --> 00:05:14,250
I apologize!

74
00:05:14,250 --> 00:05:15,750
I'll be careful in the future.

75
00:05:15,750 --> 00:05:17,210
You always say that!

76
00:05:17,210 --> 00:05:20,420
You're always insincere.
You just repeat the same thing...

77
00:05:21,710 --> 00:05:25,880
The fact is you haven't changed at all
from who you were three years ago...

78
00:05:25,880 --> 00:05:28,680
...when you first sunk your teeth into Griffith.

79
00:05:29,090 --> 00:05:32,850
All you care about
is swinging your sword in battle.

80
00:05:33,140 --> 00:05:35,930
You don't care at all about your men.

81
00:05:37,190 --> 00:05:38,690
You're just a mad dog!

82
00:05:41,440 --> 00:05:43,070
Say that again...

83
00:05:43,860 --> 00:05:45,530
Say that again if you dare!

84
00:05:47,360 --> 00:05:49,280
Why don't you two calm down now?

85
00:05:51,910 --> 00:05:53,040
Griffith!

86
00:05:53,580 --> 00:05:57,370
Casca, I will give Guts some advice...

87
00:06:05,050 --> 00:06:07,300
Griffith, you're too soft on him.

88
00:06:18,190 --> 00:06:21,480
You go through too much
trouble for him, sister Casca.

89
00:06:22,150 --> 00:06:24,860
He's Griffith's favorite pet.

90
00:06:24,860 --> 00:06:29,030
You just end up taking all
the blame whenever you confront him.

91
00:06:31,160 --> 00:06:35,410
Well, I'm willing to help
whenever you want to bump him off.

92
00:06:39,620 --> 00:06:40,540
Sorry.

93
00:06:41,290 --> 00:06:42,790
Damn it!

94
00:06:45,500 --> 00:06:47,880
You two fight like cats and dogs.

95
00:06:48,220 --> 00:06:51,010
Yet you've spent almost
three years in the same group.

96
00:06:54,140 --> 00:06:55,640
I care about them...

97
00:06:56,430 --> 00:06:59,480
In my own way, I do care about my men.

98
00:06:59,480 --> 00:07:01,690
I'm not who I was in the past.

99
00:07:03,440 --> 00:07:05,020
It takes me back...

100
00:07:05,480 --> 00:07:06,940
...to three years ago.

101
00:07:08,860 --> 00:07:11,320
You were wandering from battlefield to battlefield.

102
00:07:16,160 --> 00:07:19,410
And we had a duel
that resulted in you joining us.

103
00:07:20,660 --> 00:07:22,790
That duel was so much fun...

104
00:07:23,880 --> 00:07:26,750
That is the way duels should be.

105
00:07:29,970 --> 00:07:31,220
Come on now.

106
00:07:31,220 --> 00:07:33,390
You will be the toast of tonight's drinking.

107
00:07:35,220 --> 00:07:36,260
Griffith...

108
00:07:38,430 --> 00:07:40,020
About today's battle...

109
00:07:40,980 --> 00:07:42,310
I'm sorry.

110
00:07:43,060 --> 00:07:46,230
I drew up my battle plans
with your tendencies in mind.

111
00:07:57,870 --> 00:08:00,910
Not quarreling with some evil design...

112
00:08:01,960 --> 00:08:04,880
Not straying from virtue...

113
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:08,380
Sacrifice thyself ceaselessly...

114
00:08:08,380 --> 00:08:10,880
This is absolutely unheard of.

115
00:08:08,880 --> 00:08:12,760
Render service for peace and security.

116
00:08:10,840 --> 00:08:13,510
A mercenary granted knighthood...

117
00:08:14,130 --> 00:08:17,220
What on Earth is the king thinking?

118
00:08:14,470 --> 00:08:17,760
By the spirit of the kingdom of Midland...

119
00:08:17,760 --> 00:08:21,180
But they were a great help.

120
00:08:21,390 --> 00:08:24,270
The title of knight is bestowed on thee.

121
00:08:21,480 --> 00:08:22,310
Nonsense!

122
00:08:22,680 --> 00:08:27,020
They would be thieves without war.

123
00:08:24,270 --> 00:08:27,020
Place thy flesh and heart in heaven.

124
00:08:27,440 --> 00:08:29,900
Separate thyself from falsehood.

125
00:08:27,980 --> 00:08:30,530
Nevertheless, their services on the...

126
00:08:30,650 --> 00:08:31,940
...battlefield are necessary.

127
00:08:30,820 --> 00:08:34,450
Uphold the law, know the subjects...

128
00:08:32,360 --> 00:08:35,740
If we sit back now, we'll disappear.

129
00:08:36,110 --> 00:08:41,580
Be valiant with due courtesy and fidelity...

130
00:08:41,790 --> 00:08:44,500
They have no choice but
to acknowledge their ability.

131
00:08:44,500 --> 00:08:47,080
Because we have continuously
distinguished ourselves in battle.

132
00:08:47,080 --> 00:08:48,340
Right, Rickert?

133
00:08:49,500 --> 00:08:52,460
It's farewell to the humble mercenary life.

134
00:08:52,460 --> 00:08:55,470
We've been publicly
admitted into the regular army.

135
00:08:55,470 --> 00:08:58,640
Watch your tongue
if you know where we are, Corkus.

136
00:08:59,100 --> 00:09:00,560
We're in the middle of a ceremony.

137
00:09:01,180 --> 00:09:06,100
From now on, our behavior
could reflect badly on Griffith.

138
00:09:07,310 --> 00:09:10,520
There is no longer any excuse
to act like boorish mercenaries.

139
00:09:10,520 --> 00:09:14,700
Okay, okay, I understand,
Commander Casca, ma'am.

140
00:09:14,700 --> 00:09:16,990
She's tougher than my mom.

141
00:09:17,200 --> 00:09:18,070
What was that?

142
00:09:18,070 --> 00:09:19,700
Hey, we're at a ceremony!

143
00:09:21,160 --> 00:09:22,490
Those commoners...

144
00:09:24,370 --> 00:09:27,330
Wait a minute. He's not here again!

145
00:09:28,080 --> 00:09:29,330
One hundred ninety-five...

146
00:09:30,040 --> 00:09:31,130
One hundred ninety-six...

147
00:09:31,920 --> 00:09:33,090
One hundred ninety-seven...

148
00:09:33,880 --> 00:09:35,220
One hundred ninety-eight...

149
00:09:36,170 --> 00:09:37,260
One hundred ninety-nine...

150
00:09:38,930 --> 00:09:39,850
Two hundred!

151
00:10:39,570 --> 00:10:41,570
Thanks for scouting, Judeau.

152
00:10:41,570 --> 00:10:44,740
So what's going on
at the enemy's supply base?

153
00:10:45,160 --> 00:10:48,160
Their defense focuses on this side,
so our information was correct.

154
00:10:48,870 --> 00:10:50,830
It's not much of a force though.

155
00:10:51,380 --> 00:10:55,050
If so, we should try
to outflank them or something.

156
00:10:55,050 --> 00:10:56,250
No...

157
00:10:56,250 --> 00:10:57,670
We attack them from the front.

158
00:10:58,970 --> 00:11:00,380
But that's dangerous!

159
00:11:00,930 --> 00:11:05,850
Our objective is to capture the enemy
supply base as soon as possible.

160
00:11:06,770 --> 00:11:11,190
We could probably reach the armory
swiftly by attacking from behind...

161
00:11:11,190 --> 00:11:14,560
However, we'd also draw
the garrison to the armory if we did.

162
00:11:15,270 --> 00:11:18,780
In that case, it'd take more time
to completely occupy the fort.

163
00:11:19,110 --> 00:11:20,610
I see...

164
00:11:20,610 --> 00:11:25,740
To thin the fort's guard, we should
attack the front of the supply base.

165
00:11:26,080 --> 00:11:27,120
Yes.

166
00:11:27,120 --> 00:11:28,200
Additionally...

167
00:11:28,660 --> 00:11:30,910
We'll deal with the armory as soon as possible.

168
00:11:30,910 --> 00:11:34,580
Be extremely careful after breaking
through the fort's central gate.

169
00:11:35,250 --> 00:11:37,380
So what's our formation?

170
00:11:37,800 --> 00:11:41,630
First, Guts and Casca's companies
will attract the garrisons' attention.

171
00:11:42,050 --> 00:11:44,850
The main company will ride into
the fort and break through the front.

172
00:11:45,300 --> 00:11:46,600
I got it.

173
00:11:46,600 --> 00:11:49,270
As soon as the preparations
are complete, we'll start the operation.

174
00:11:51,440 --> 00:11:52,850
Oh boy...

175
00:11:52,850 --> 00:11:56,190
Guts will end up snatching the credit again!

176
00:11:57,230 --> 00:11:59,780
Hey, you want to argue with me?

177
00:12:02,860 --> 00:12:03,910
Casca!

178
00:12:03,910 --> 00:12:05,410
Griffith gave those orders!

179
00:12:12,790 --> 00:12:15,000
We are no longer mercenaries.

180
00:12:15,790 --> 00:12:17,340
Keep that in mind.

181
00:12:19,960 --> 00:12:23,010
Look, if you go off on your own again...

182
00:12:23,630 --> 00:12:24,760
...you will...

183
00:12:29,060 --> 00:12:29,600
Guts!

184
00:12:33,270 --> 00:12:34,690
I'm depending on you, Casca.

185
00:13:24,190 --> 00:13:25,360
Why should I...

186
00:13:26,030 --> 00:13:29,950
...I, the leader of the Blue Whale
Heavy Assault Knights, Sir Adon...

187
00:13:29,950 --> 00:13:33,910
Why do I have to patrol this miserable
supply base and its armory?

188
00:13:33,910 --> 00:13:36,830
Sir, it's because the Black Ram Heavy Cavalry...

189
00:13:36,830 --> 00:13:39,840
...was crippled, so we were
installed here as a substitute.

190
00:13:40,170 --> 00:13:41,040
Hush!

191
00:13:41,040 --> 00:13:42,170
I know that!

192
00:13:43,630 --> 00:13:47,930
It's beneath one of the glorious
Coborlwitz family to be in this mission.

193
00:13:47,930 --> 00:13:48,550
Damn!

194
00:13:51,600 --> 00:13:52,510
What is it?

195
00:13:52,890 --> 00:13:54,720
Well, I see something...

196
00:13:57,190 --> 00:13:57,810
Hey!

197
00:14:05,440 --> 00:14:06,440
Commander Adon!

198
00:14:06,740 --> 00:14:08,910
It's an enemy raid!

199
00:14:08,910 --> 00:14:10,200
Don't be foolish!

200
00:14:10,200 --> 00:14:13,160
Who on Earth would bother
to attack such a remote supply base?

201
00:14:14,700 --> 00:14:15,910
W-What?

202
00:14:39,310 --> 00:14:40,600
T-This is...

203
00:14:41,520 --> 00:14:43,570
Don't fall back!

204
00:14:45,610 --> 00:14:47,070
You son of a bitch!

205
00:14:53,370 --> 00:14:54,160
C-Commander!

206
00:15:21,810 --> 00:15:22,480
Shit!

207
00:15:27,150 --> 00:15:28,360
He's doing it again!

208
00:15:28,740 --> 00:15:29,990
Hold it, Guts!

209
00:15:29,990 --> 00:15:31,360
Did you forget our duty?

210
00:15:31,660 --> 00:15:32,780
Get out of my way!

211
00:15:34,530 --> 00:15:35,330
Guts!

212
00:15:38,700 --> 00:15:39,500
Griffith!

213
00:15:41,120 --> 00:15:42,170
It's a trap!

214
00:15:42,170 --> 00:15:43,040
Turn around!

215
00:15:43,630 --> 00:15:44,250
What?

216
00:15:48,340 --> 00:15:49,340
Retreat!

217
00:15:52,010 --> 00:15:52,880
Retreat?

218
00:15:52,880 --> 00:15:54,010
That can't be!

219
00:15:54,510 --> 00:15:55,640
Hurry up, Corkus!

220
00:16:01,600 --> 00:16:02,640
What the hell?

221
00:16:13,530 --> 00:16:14,700
Take shelter!

222
00:16:24,250 --> 00:16:27,590
That was my special fleeing technique, Bakuretsu Funsai!

223
00:16:27,590 --> 00:16:30,300
It's been handed down through
the Coborlwitz family for 300 years!

224
00:16:30,670 --> 00:16:34,590
B-But the fort... Our key supply base is...

225
00:16:34,590 --> 00:16:35,640
Shut up!

226
00:16:35,640 --> 00:16:36,180
Quit yapping!

227
00:16:37,100 --> 00:16:39,060
Now withdraw the troops!

228
00:16:48,520 --> 00:16:50,650
Is everyone all right?

229
00:16:55,990 --> 00:16:58,200
I'm glad everyone is okay!

230
00:16:58,200 --> 00:17:00,290
It's thanks to Guts.

231
00:17:30,150 --> 00:17:33,110
But really, that explosion was something else!

232
00:17:33,110 --> 00:17:36,360
All the spoils were destroyed.

233
00:17:36,650 --> 00:17:37,860
It's no big deal.

234
00:17:37,860 --> 00:17:41,410
We were able to achieve our objective
and damage the enemy supply base.

235
00:17:41,410 --> 00:17:43,500
What are you talking about?

236
00:17:43,500 --> 00:17:45,790
You are totally an amateur, kid.

237
00:17:45,790 --> 00:17:47,080
Sorry I'm young!

238
00:17:47,620 --> 00:17:49,380
What's bothering you?

239
00:17:52,250 --> 00:17:54,920
Get to the point, if you have something to say!

240
00:17:54,920 --> 00:17:57,090
It's not like you to hesitate!

241
00:17:57,090 --> 00:17:58,010
Shut up!

242
00:17:58,010 --> 00:17:59,050
I just...

243
00:18:01,010 --> 00:18:06,520
I just want to say that your
actions in battle today were right.

244
00:18:06,940 --> 00:18:09,980
I just did whatever I wanted, like always.

245
00:18:09,980 --> 00:18:11,560
It's different!

246
00:18:11,560 --> 00:18:14,480
You were just desperately
trying to protect Griffith.

247
00:18:14,480 --> 00:18:16,440
But I didn't understand that...

248
00:18:19,990 --> 00:18:20,990
So...

249
00:18:21,410 --> 00:18:22,450
I mean...

250
00:18:25,410 --> 00:18:26,870
I'm sorry.

251
00:18:47,930 --> 00:18:52,650
Midland's troops were like ants attacking me.

252
00:18:52,650 --> 00:18:55,110
I completely defeated them.

253
00:18:55,530 --> 00:19:00,360
So did you confirm that
they were totally destroyed?

254
00:19:00,570 --> 00:19:03,830
Of course I did, General Boscone!

255
00:19:16,750 --> 00:19:17,760
You buffoon!

256
00:19:18,720 --> 00:19:22,140
They are alive, and they occupy the supply base!

257
00:19:22,140 --> 00:19:24,140
H-How could it be?

258
00:19:24,430 --> 00:19:25,720
Get lost!

259
00:19:25,720 --> 00:19:28,890
Waste no time in undoing
this disgrace to the empire!

260
00:19:29,230 --> 00:19:30,730
Y-Yes, sir!

261
00:19:34,110 --> 00:19:36,270
Calm down.

262
00:19:40,030 --> 00:19:41,780
Governor Gennon...

263
00:19:41,780 --> 00:19:45,700
The loss of a supply base
changes nothing in the overall war.

264
00:19:45,700 --> 00:19:49,540
However, we must inflict
a crushing defeat on those insects.

265
00:19:49,540 --> 00:19:53,710
Especially the impertinent Band of the Hawk...

266
00:19:54,040 --> 00:19:55,170
Band of the Hawk?

267
00:19:55,920 --> 00:19:57,590
What's wrong?

268
00:19:59,510 --> 00:20:00,970
Never mind...

269
00:20:06,510 --> 00:20:08,060
Leave it to them?

270
00:20:08,680 --> 00:20:13,390
Yes, I will trust them with
our next offensive's siege.

271
00:20:14,230 --> 00:20:16,110
Excuse me, Your Majesty...

272
00:20:16,110 --> 00:20:19,570
...but can we charge such boorish
troops with so important a mission?

273
00:20:19,780 --> 00:20:21,110
I agree with him.

274
00:20:21,110 --> 00:20:23,530
My army would lead
the offensive if we were allowed...

275
00:20:23,950 --> 00:20:25,530
Could I count on you?

276
00:20:26,950 --> 00:20:33,000
Do you have perfect
confidence in your ability to win?

277
00:20:35,120 --> 00:20:37,290
My intentions will not change.

278
00:20:38,040 --> 00:20:39,630
Send word to Griffith.

279
00:20:39,630 --> 00:20:43,470
When the preparations are finished,
they will take the field immediately.

280
00:20:43,470 --> 00:20:44,340
Of course!

281
00:22:03,390 --> 00:22:05,850
Looking back, the morning comes.

282
00:22:05,850 --> 00:22:09,350
Don't find your face in your glass.

283
00:22:10,390 --> 00:22:13,480
Take the moonlight by the tail.

284
00:22:13,480 --> 00:22:16,440
It's a rainy sight. You're shading.

285
00:22:17,900 --> 00:22:19,650
What is that?

286
00:22:19,650 --> 00:22:20,900
It's just the same.

287
00:22:20,900 --> 00:22:24,070
What is trying your crown?

288
00:22:25,160 --> 00:22:28,370
I'm spending my glass, walking back.

289
00:22:28,370 --> 00:22:31,410
So wear my glass. You're fading.

290
00:22:31,710 --> 00:22:51,310
I'm waiting so long.

291
00:22:51,310 --> 00:23:00,400
I'm waiting...

